(1, 6, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'The peritoneal membrane is made up of _____cell layers', '["4", "1", "3", "2"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: 2.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 7, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'The ______ of the peritoneal membrane account for greater than 90% of solute removal.', '["Capillary endothelium", "Large pore", "Ultra small pore", "Small pore"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Small pore.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 8, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'In which year was peritoneal dialysis first used for the management of ESRD?', '["1960", "1959", "1957", "1989"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: 1959.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 9, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Icodextrin can cause falsely high glucose readings with:', '["All laboratory tests", "Urine dipsticks only", "Some glucose meters (GDH-PQQ method)", "Blood pressure monitors"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Use a glucose-specific method.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 10, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'The Tenckhoff catheter has cuffs that:', '["Anchor it and reduce infection tracking along the tunnel", "Warm the dialysate", "Measure fluid volume", "Connect to the bladder"]'::jsonb, 0, 'It is the standard PD catheter.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 11, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Sirolimus (an mTOR inhibitor) may cause:', '["Gum hyperplasia", "Poor wound healing and high lipids", "Bradycardia", "Low cholesterol"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It is often started after the wound has healed.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 12, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Glucose absorbed from PD fluid can lead to:', '["Weight loss and hypoglycaemia", "Low cholesterol", "Weight gain, hyperglycaemia and high triglycerides", "Hypokalaemia only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Diet and glucose control need adjusting.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 13, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A transplant recipient should report immediately:', '["Normal urine output", "Improved appetite", "Feeling well", "Fever, reduced urine, graft pain or swelling"]'::jsonb, 3, 'These may signal rejection or infection.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 14, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'New-onset diabetes after transplant is linked mainly to:', '["Co-trimoxazole", "Tacrolimus and steroids", "Iron supplements", "Mycophenolate"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Screen glucose regularly.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 15, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'CRRT filter life is shortened by:', '["Correct blood flow", "Low blood flow, high haematocrit and poor anticoagulation", "Pre-dilution replacement fluid", "Good anticoagulation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Frequent filter clotting wastes blood.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 16, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A newly inserted PD catheter is usually rested (not used) for about:', '["2 weeks to allow healing", "1 day", "1 hour", "6 months"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Urgent-start PD uses small supine volumes.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 17, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Icodextrin PD solution is useful for:', '["Short 30-minute dwells only", "Long dwells, such as the overnight CAPD or daytime APD dwell", "Raising blood glucose", "Treating peritonitis"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It gives sustained ultrafiltration.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 18, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A standard CAPD regimen is usually:', '["One exchange a month", "One exchange a week", "About four exchanges a day, each of about 2 litres", "Twenty exchanges a day"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Each exchange takes about 30–40 minutes.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 19, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Hypokalaemia is common in PD patients because:', '["Potassium is lost continuously and PD fluid contains no potassium", "They eat too much potassium", "They are always on dialysis in hospital", "PD fluid is high in potassium"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Some need potassium supplements.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 20, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Residual kidney function in dialysis patients is important because it:', '["Improves survival, fluid and phosphate control", "Prevents peritonitis", "Increases potassium", "Has no value"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Avoid nephrotoxins and hypotension.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 21, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Conservative kidney management (non-dialysis care) is suitable for:', '["All patients with stage 2 CKD", "Elderly frail patients who choose not to have dialysis", "Young fit patients wanting transplant", "Patients with AKI who will recover"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It focuses on symptom control and quality of life.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 22, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Hydrothorax in a PD patient is caused by:', '["Kidney stones", "Dialysate passing through a diaphragmatic defect into the chest", "Fluid overload from drinking", "Heart failure only"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It usually affects the right side.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 23, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'BK virus in kidney transplant recipients can cause:', '["Pneumonia only", "Hepatitis", "Nephropathy and graft dysfunction", "Meningitis"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Reduce immunosuppression if detected.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 24, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'After kidney transplantation, the patient''s blood group must be:', '["Different from the donor in all cases", "Checked only after surgery", "ABO compatible with the donor, or managed with special protocols", "Unimportant"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Cross-matching checks for antibodies.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 25, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A hernia in a PD patient is caused by:', '["Fistula surgery", "Low potassium", "Raised intra-abdominal pressure from the dialysate", "Low blood pressure"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Small fill volumes or supine APD may help.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 26, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'During CRRT, the patient should be monitored for:', '["Hypoglycaemia only", "Hyperthermia only", "Weight gain only", "Hypothermia, electrolyte changes and bleeding"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Use a fluid warmer if needed.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 27, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Automated peritoneal dialysis (APD) is done:', '["Overnight using a cycler machine", "Only in hospital ICU", "Through a fistula", "Using a blood pump"]'::jsonb, 0, 'It frees the day for school or work.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 28, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Withdrawal from dialysis usually leads to death within about:', '["1–2 weeks", "1 day", "6 months", "5 years"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Palliative care should support the patient and family.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 29, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Pain during the inflow of PD fluid may be relieved by:', '["Stopping all exchanges forever", "Increasing the bag height", "Using cold fluid", "Slowing the inflow and ensuring the fluid is warm"]'::jsonb, 3, 'It often settles after the first weeks.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 30, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Peritoneal dialysis adequacy is assessed with:', '["Serum amylase", "Daily chest X-rays", "Weekly Kt/V urea and creatinine clearance, plus clinical well-being", "Blood cultures"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A weekly Kt/V of at least 1.7 is a common target.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 31, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Mycophenolate mofetil commonly causes:', '["Hypertension only", "Diarrhoea and low white cell count", "Hair growth", "Gum overgrowth"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It is avoided in pregnancy.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 32, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A positive cross-match before transplant means:', '["The donor is healthy", "The kidney is a perfect match", "The recipient has antibodies against donor cells, so transplant is high risk", "Immunosuppression is not needed"]'::jsonb, 2, 'It predicts hyperacute rejection.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 33, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Cyclosporine can cause:', '["Hair loss and weight loss", "Low blood pressure", "Hypoglycaemia", "Gum hyperplasia, hirsutism, hypertension and nephrotoxicity"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Levels must be monitored.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 34, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'In peritoneal dialysis, ultrafiltration is driven mainly by:', '["The blood pump", "The patient''s heart rate", "The osmotic gradient from glucose (or icodextrin) in the dialysate", "Hydrostatic pressure from the machine only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Higher glucose strengths remove more fluid.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 35, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Pneumocystis jirovecii prophylaxis after kidney transplant is usually with:', '["Insulin", "Paracetamol", "Co-trimoxazole", "Furosemide"]'::jsonb, 2, 'It is given for the first months.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 36, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Paediatric peritoneal dialysis fill volumes are calculated by:', '["Height only", "Adult standard 2 L for all", "Body surface area (e.g. about 1000–1200 mL/m²)", "Age only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Too large volumes cause discomfort and hernia.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 37, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Plasmapheresis (plasma exchange) is used in conditions such as:', '["Benign prostate enlargement", "Kidney stones", "Goodpasture syndrome and some vasculitis", "Simple UTI"]'::jsonb, 2, 'It removes harmful antibodies from the blood.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 38, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'A living kidney donor must be assessed for:', '["Only blood group", "Normal kidney function, health and voluntary consent", "Only their wealth", "Only their age"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Donor safety comes first.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 39, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Swimming for PD patients is:', '["Always forbidden", "Safe in rivers and lakes", "Allowed without covering the exit site", "Only in clean sea or chlorinated private pools with a waterproof dressing, if allowed"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Rivers and lakes carry infection risk.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 40, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'Poor outflow of PD fluid is often relieved by:', '["Treating constipation and changing the patient''s position", "Using cold dialysate", "Giving antihypertensives", "Increasing protein intake"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Catheter displacement may need X-ray.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
(1, 41, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II', 'Which among the following is not factors that contribute to renal agenesis?', '["Bacteria", "Environment", "Family history", "Genetics"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Bacteria.', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II'),
(1, 42, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II', 'In metabolic acidosis, which of the following is commonly prescribed to neutralize acid in the body?', '["Magnesium sulfate", "Calcium carbonate", "Sodium bicarbonate", "Potassium chloride"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Sodium bicarbonate is used to correct acidosis by neutralizing excess acid.', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II'),
(1, 43, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II', 'Which of the following is a primary glomerular disease?', '["Chronic glomerulonephritis", "Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)", "Haemolytic-uremic syndrome", "Diabetic glomerulopathy"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Chronic glomerulonephritis.', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II'),
(1, 44, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II', 'Kidney plays important roles in matainance of haemostasis failure to it can lead to collection of symptoms as a result of kidney damage which affect both children and adult respectively.', '["Obstructive uropathy", "Nephrotic syndrome", "UTI", "Glomerular Nephritis"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Nephrotic syndrome.', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II'),
(1, 45, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 4 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II', 'When calculating urine output in a patient recovering from AKI, the nurse should:', '["Monitor only intake and ignore output", "Measure and document hourly output", "Track daily serum potassium", "Document creatinine levels only"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Measure and document hourly output.', 'NNP 421 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology II'),
